1
00:00:00,102 --> 00:00:01,812
(Leonard:)Seconded.

2
00:00:02,312 --> 00:00:04,652
I was gonna put down a towel.

3
00:00:07,818 --> 00:00:11,738
(Raj:)I still want it on my balcony.
I say we move it on a bimonthly basis.

4
00:00:11,905 --> 00:00:14,865
- That sounds fair.
- Hold on. Bimonthly is an ambiguous term.

5
00:00:15,033 --> 00:00:17,663
(Sheldon:)- Every other month or twice a month?
- Twice a month.

6
00:00:17,828 --> 00:00:19,828
- Then no.
- Okay, every other month.

7
00:00:19,996 --> 00:00:21,536
(Sheldon:)No.

8
00:00:22,290 --> 00:00:23,750
(Leonard:)Sheldon, you can't be selfish.

9
00:00:23,917 --> 00:00:26,257
(Leonard:)We all paid for it,
so it belongs to all of us.

10
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:29,380
Now get out of the way
so I can sit in my time machine.

11
00:00:34,010 --> 00:00:36,010
[ALL GASPING]

12
00:00:37,973 --> 00:00:43,103
(Leonard:)Okay. I am setting the dials
for March 10th, 1876.

13
00:00:43,270 --> 00:00:46,860
(Howard:)Good choice. Alexander Graham Bell
invents the telephone and calls for Watson.

14
00:00:47,023 --> 00:00:50,523
- Wait a minute. I wanna see that too.
- So when it's your turn, you can.

15
00:00:50,694 --> 00:00:54,194
If we all go back to the same time,
Bell's lab's going to get very crowded.

16
00:00:54,364 --> 00:00:56,364
(Sheldon:)He'll know something's up.

17
00:00:56,533 --> 00:00:58,703
(Raj:)Since the time machine
doesn't move in space...

18
00:00:58,869 --> 00:01:02,039
(Raj:)- ...you'll end up in 1876 Pasadena.
- Even if you make it to Boston...

